URL:https://jackofthewood.com/events/charming-disaster/
SUMMARY:Charming Disaster
DESCRIPTION:\nKick of Halloween weekend with an extremely special treat\, b
 rought to you live here at Jack of the Wood!Brooklyn-based musical duo Cha
 rming Disaster was formed in 2012 by Ellia Bisker and Jeff Morris. Inspire
 d by the gothic humor of Edward Gorey and Tim Burton\, the murder ballads 
 of the Americana tradition\, and the dramatic flair of the cabaret\, they 
 write songs that tell stories\, using two voices to explore dark narrative
 s and characters with a playfully macabre sensibility.\n\n\n\nIn their int
 eractive Musical Oracle show\, songs are selected by chance by audience me
 mbers who draw cards from the Charming Disaster Oracle Deck—a Tarot-styl
 e divination that straddles the line between concert and theatre. \n\n\n\n
 Charming Disaster has released seven critically acclaimed albums: Love\, C
 rime &amp\; Other Trouble (2015)\, Cautionary Tales (2017)\, SPELLS + RITU
 ALS (2019)\, Our Lady of Radium (2022)\, Super Natural History (2023)\, si
 ngles collection Time Ghost (2024)\, and The Double (2025). In their songs
 \, the duo have explored love\, death\, crime\, folklore\, mythology\, mag
 ic\, science\, and the occult. Their theatrical live performances combine 
 vocal harmonies and clever lyrics with ukulele\, guitar\, and virtuosic fo
 ot percussion\, drawing listeners into a spooky\, offbeat universe of para
 normal romance\, con artists\, circus performers\, ancient mythology\, nig
 htclubs\, car chases\, the afterlife\, and beyond. \n\n\n\nCharming Disast
 er’s music has been featured on the podcast Welcome to Night Vale\, they
  have opened for legendary cello-rock ensemble Rasputina\, goth icon Volta
 ire\, and punk cabaret duo The Dresden Dolls\, and their theatrical\, ente
 rtaining live performances have captivated audiences across the United Sta
 tes and Europe. They have played festivals\, bars and clubs\, museums and 
 art galleries\, bookstores and libraries\, and the occasional historic cem
 etery. They have appeared alongside storytellers\, comedians\, fire eaters
 \, puppets\, burlesque artists\, poets\, and circus performers. Recent app
 earances include the Meadowlark Festival\, the Rochester Fringe Festival\,
  Dragon Con\, Joe’s Pub at The Public Theater in NYC\, Brooklyn’s hist
 oric Green-Wood Cemetery\, Philadelphia’s Science History Institute\, th
 e Edgar Allan Poe Museum in Richmond\, VA\, Cleveland’s Wizbang Theatre\
 , and the Coney Island Sideshow stage.Opening will be TOYBOX: An inexplica
 ble blend of comedy\, storytelling\, puppetry and clowning with Toybox\, A
 merica's Favorite Cartoon Witch! Toybox is a multiple award winning artist
  and has been described as "One of the most unique performers working toda
 y". His accolades include\, Fan Favorite and Best Performance at the Natio
 nal Puppetry Festival\, Funniest and Fringiest at The Asheville Fringe Fes
 tival\, funding from The Jim Henson Foundation\, and an UNIMA Citation of 
 Excellence In The Art of Puppetry\, the highest honor given in the field.\
 n\n\n\nMusic 8:30-11:30pm\, $10 cover at the door. Buy advanced tickets HE
 RE.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TAjqTD8kFNI\n\n\n\n\n
 \nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BNIzpoFj4a0&amp\;t=20s\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n
 \n\n\n\n\n
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://jackofthewood.com/wp-content/uploads/202
 6/09/10-30-26_CharmingDisaster_IG_1080x1440_RVSD.jpg
END:VEVENT
